  "sn22.87:10.6": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Vivatta</i> (or <i lang='pi' translate='no'>vivaṭṭa</i>) often means “cast off”, as in “the fetters” (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>vivattayi saṁyojanaṁ</i>) or the “veil” (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>vivaṭṭacchada</i>). Here it describes the dead monk’s body after attaining final Nibbāna. ",
